Use io, list, and math.

Define function cmp_i64 taking a as a pointer to whole number and b as a pointer to whole number returning a whole number:
    If value at a is less than value at b, give back -1.
    If value at a is more than value at b, give back 1.
    Give back 0.
Done.

Define function permute_unique taking nums as a pointer to List of whole number, chosen as a pointer to List of whole number, used as a pointer to List of whole number, n as an unsigned number:
    Let chosen count be count of chosen.
    If chosen count equals n:
        For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
            Say list_get(chosen, i).
        Say "---".
        Give back.
    For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
        Let used flag be list_get(used, i).
        If used flag is 0:
            Let skip be false.
            If i is more than 0:
                Let prior be list_get(nums, i - 1).
                Let current be list_get(nums, i).
                Let prior used be list_get(used, i - 1).
                If current equals prior and prior used is 0:
                    Set skip to true.
            If skip is false:
                list_set(used, i, 1).
                push list_get(nums, i) to chosen.
                permute_unique(nums, chosen, used, n).
                Let ignored value be pop from chosen.
                list_set(used, i, 0).
Done.

Let nums be a list of 1, 1, and 2.
sort address of nums using function cmp_i64.
Let n be count of nums.
Let chosen be an empty list of whole numbers.
Let used be an empty list of whole numbers.
For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    push 0 to address of used.
permute_unique(address of nums, address of chosen, address of used, n).
list_free(address of used).
list_free(address of chosen).
list_free(address of nums).
Return 0.
